@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://www.glossarist.org/dpp/dataset/dpp/concept/dpp-0140>
  a skos:Concept ;
  skos:notation "dpp-0140" ;
  skos:prefLabel "predicate-based recall"@eng ;
  skos:definition "recall scheme in which the recall set is never enumerated centrally: the recall predicate is published, and each custodian evaluates it locally against their own holdings — including dark and defence holdings under national procedure — and acts"@eng ;
  skos:scopeNote "The manufacturer receives aggregates or nothing; there is no traversal-push enumeration of the installed base."@eng ;
  skos:scopeNote "One of the mechanisms by which enumeration resistance (concept dpp-0139) is maintained: recall propagation still notifies custodians transitively, but through local predicate evaluation rather than central construction of the recall set."@eng
 .